WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.850
Many of you have been holding off on buying
the budget $329 iPad because of rumors of

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:11.910
new 2019 iPads coming soon, and now, they’re
finally here, the 2019 iPad Mini 5 for $400

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:15.169
and 2019 iPad Air for $500.

00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:20.160
The new Mini may not be that bad of a deal,
but the new Air is extremely underwhelming,

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.510
and anyone looking for a new budget iPad should
not buy it.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.609
I repeat, don’t buy the 2019 iPad Air.

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:30.759
I’ll give you all my personal recommendation
on what to buy in just a minute.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:36.250
Ultimately, it’s a handicapped version of
the 2017 10.5” iPad Pro.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:43.061
It’s using the same chassis, display resolution,
battery, Apple Pencil support, and more, but

00:00:43.061 --> 00:00:47.240
although it seems like it’s just as good,
it’s missing some very important components

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.240
of the Pro.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.420
So here are 5 things that are lacking compared
to the 10.5” iPad Pro.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.960
The first two have to do with the display.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.100
First of all, the display brightness is limited
to 500 nits instead of the Pros 600 nits,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.809
so it’s quite a bit dimmer and it doesn’t
support HDR video, even though it supports

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:06.210
P3 wide color gamut.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.680
Secondly, it doesn’t support ProMotion,
which is the one thing that made the iPad

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:11.680
Pro so great.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:17.710
It basically doubles the screens refresh rate
to 120hz so every swipe and animation is buttery

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.710
smooth.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:21.640
Trust me, this makes a massive difference
in day-to-day use.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:27.000
Not only that, but ProMotion also significantly
reduces Apple Pencil input lag, making it

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.390
seem like you’re drawing on actual paper.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:32.300
The new Air really misses out big by lacking
ProMotion.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:36.340
The third thing isn’t that big of a deal
for an iPad, but it still sucks.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:42.170
The rear camera is only 8MP compared to 12
on the iPad Pro, so you don’t get 4K video

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:47.230
recording or 1080P at 60, and picture quality
is gonna be worse as well.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:51.740
For the 4th thing, the new iPad Air only has
one set of speakers on the bottom compared

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:54.420
to four speakers on the 10.5” Pro.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.590
The speakers were both louder and the stereo
sound in landscape mode was amazing compared

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.380
to the old 2-speaker setup.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.590
All in all, the new air is just lacking way
too much for me to be able to recommend it.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:10.009
Yes, it’s got an A12 processor that’s
more powerful than the A10X, but to completely

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:14.981
honest, it was already tough to notice the
difference between the A10X and the A12X in

00:02:14.981 --> 00:02:18.209
the new iPad Pro, at least in day-to-day use.

00:02:18.209 --> 00:02:23.660
The A10X in the 10.5” Pro can run basically
any app or game currently available on the

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.680
market, so the A12 doesn’t make that big
of a difference.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:30.730
Now you might be saying, of course, the Pro
is better, that’s why it’s called the

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:31.730
Pro.

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:37.870
Well, in reality, Apple was selling it for
$650, only $150 more than the new Air, and

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:42.129
it was definitely worth it, just for the ProMotion
technology alone.

00:02:42.129 --> 00:02:47.459
Unfortunately, Apple took it off their website
this morning, as soon as the new Air was available,

00:02:47.459 --> 00:02:48.459
and we all know why.

00:02:48.459 --> 00:02:54.499
Now here’s the good news, you can easily
find a used 10.5” iPad Pro for under $500,

00:02:54.499 --> 00:02:59.450
or refurbished models on Amazon with prime
shipping for only $434.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:03.409
You can even get a brand new one on sale for
only $570 on Amazon.

00:03:03.409 --> 00:03:04.540
So that’s my recommendation.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.279
if you’re thinking of getting the new Air,
don’t.

00:03:07.279 --> 00:03:09.340
Buy a used 10.5” Pro instead.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.040
You’ll be much more happy with it.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.359
Now if you’re not looking to spend that
much money, the 2018 iPad for $329 is still

00:03:16.359 --> 00:03:18.489
the best deal for an iPad ever.

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:22.230
It’s good enough for almost everyone and
I still recommend it for anyone that isn’t

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.999
looking to buy the new 2018 iPad Pro.

00:03:24.999 --> 00:03:29.959
Even better, I’ve seen it on sale on Amazon
for as little as $250 brand new.

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:31.409
You simply can’t beat that value.

00:03:31.409 --> 00:03:35.489
Now let’s say you’ve been waiting a while
and you really want a new iPad, but can’t

00:03:35.489 --> 00:03:36.769
afford the new Pro.

00:03:36.769 --> 00:03:40.239
Well, the new iPad Mini actually isn’t a
bad deal.

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:45.010
It’s got everything the new Air has, but
with a smaller display for $100 less.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:48.349
But it’s really meant to be in a market
of its own, for those who want that smaller

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:50.069
display and portability.

00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:56.279
I honestly still recommend going for the budget
2018 iPad unless you’re buying the new 2018

00:03:56.279 --> 00:03:57.279
iPad Pro.

00:03:57.279 --> 00:04:01.510
If you haven’t seen our 1-year review of
the 2018 iPad, click the card above or click

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.560
the end screen button at the end of this video.

